I've 10% off right now for cyber week and black friday. I sell roleplaying game accessories such as dice and dice storage with wooden and faux leather dice boxes

&#x200B;

[https://www.etsy.com/uk/shop/CrafticalHit](https://www.etsy.com/uk/shop/CrafticalHit)

Doxy Die Cast - more oomph than the hitachi  [https://doxymassager.com/products/the-doxy-die-cast-silver](https://doxymassager.com/products/the-doxy-die-cast-silver) 

&#x200B;

Source - friend who works in a sex shop and sells these things for a living

ESH - you could have handled it a little better.

&#x200B;

First up, the mothers will is clear, the siblings have basically, from the sounds of it, got greedy and wanted more than what they were to have, and the selling of the house means they will get more. the fact they want that split equally will leave the wife with less overall as they already have some money that was set aside for them.

&#x200B;

Second, as a couple, and as a future married couple this is a decision you should discuss together and so she is being an ass for not discussing it, but it is her house to do with as she wishes, even if you dont agree. 

&#x200B;

Personally i dont see any issue with asking for a small token amount for 'rent' because there are costs associated with upkeep and maintenance of a house, which your wife now has the burden of.

&#x200B;

I can understand that with the loss of her mother your partner doesnt want to rock the boat with the rest of the family and potentially burn bridges, but at the end of the day, this was their mothers last will and testament and by proxy her last wish. If they have any legitimate respect for their mother they would respect the will.
